  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "Cleaning Upwards for a Decade\nAt the turn of the millennium, India's crude oil refinery capacity stood at just over 1 mbd, and was a net importer of clean petroleum products. Now, following a decade of aggressive growth, India is seated within the top five countries in terms of refinery capacity and is a net exporter of refined petroleum products. Refining giant Reliance Industries is one of the driving forces behind this remarkable transformation, currently accountable for roughly 1.2 mbd or 42% of India's capacity.",
